{
 "about": "Per-state tables of the US answer key (kpc_us_key.py reads this file at start; a missing or malformed file stops the build: nothing is written). Moved out of the rule script on Nov 12 (KPC owner, 2026-11-12; D6), unchanged in content. BOX_ADD = land the drawn state outline (kpc-us-states.json) leaves out: [west, south, east, north] added to the state's box. XS = official agency layers read for the listed states ONLY (areas), each stored once; kpc_area_hash.py counts an entry for every state it lists. Fields: prefix (record-id prefix, never reuse one), url (query url, or svc:<service>|<layer-name regex>), name_field / acres_field ('?' = found at run time), kinds, label, owner (STAT / FED), options (where, water, nm2, not_in). Order: the national layers in the code are read first, then these in file order; 'after' = read right after that national layer instead (kept so the read order is exactly what it was). notes = where each entry came from (not read by the builder, not in any hash).",
 "format": 1,
 "notes": {
  "FL": [
   "BOX_ADD.FL, Nov 11 (KPC owner, 2026-11-11): kpc-us-states.json draws Florida without the Keys (south edge 25.12), so every Florida box read missed Monroe County (FL DEP state-owned lands: 2,545 Keys parcels). The box takes in the Keys and the Dry Tortugas. Nov 11 r3 (run 43037613117): the east edge moved from -80.0 to -79.8 (45 FL DEP parcels off Miami; Bimini, the nearest Bahamas land, is at -79.3; Cay Sal Bank is south of 24.3)."
  ],
  "HI": [
   "XS akht, Oct 26 (round 11): the NPS Ala Kahakai National Historic Trail official corridor (one polygon)."
  ],
  "*": [
   "XS state layers: Oct 18 (owner: 'go ahead'): the state agencies' own land maps (owner = the agency) for states with many unmatched parks; Oct 20: probe rounds 2 and 4 (owner = the state agency / state GIS office)."
  ]
 },
